videos.script:
During a study session, the planner should keep the screen on. None of the official plugins does that. {{need}}

So today you write a plugin. But first, the questions to ask before writing one. {{questions}} Can the web do it already? Is there an official plugin? A community one? A plugin of your own is native code you maintain on two platforms, for years.

Then the plugin itself. {{generate}} Capacitor's generator writes the project. You write an interface in TypeScript, and three implementations of it. {{three}} One for the browser, with the Screen Wake Lock API. One in Kotlin for Android. One in Swift for iOS. A single name joins them, and the lesson shows what breaks when it does not match. {{name}}

Last, the planner installs it like any other package, and two new buttons keep the screen on, and let it sleep again. {{buttons}}
